  "findings": [
    "Partial pooling materially reduces error versus trusting noisy first-half percentages at face value.",
    "The largest gains come from lower-volume shooters, whose observed rates carry the most sampling noise.",
    "Shrinkage wins across the cohort, but it can underpredict established high-skill shooters; player-level misses still need basketball context."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The evaluation cohort requires at least 25 three-point attempts in each half, so it excludes many low-usage and injured players.",
    "The model uses makes and attempts only; role, shot quality, injuries, lineup context, and tracking data are not available.",
    "This is a single-season backtest. A production forecast should repeat the design across multiple seasons before deployment."
  ]
